So why naga and why rust directly in the source?

Well, dawn requires C++20 to compile source and headers.
That's a no go.

I wish naga had some sort of C/C++ bindings but it doesn't.
I could create a brand new repository for this, but I really don't want to.
In the future, there should be some third-party naga-sys or libnaga crate that replaces this.

Use cargo build (without --release) to compile this.
